@startuml sd_us210
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
title US210 - Sequence Diagram
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
actor "Backoffice Operator" as Actor
participant "Entry (Envoy)\nvirtual IP of airports-routes" as EAR
box "airports-routes-n (the replica that answers)" #F7F7F7
participant "AirportController" as AirportController
participant "GetAirportStatisticsUseCase" as GetAirportStatisticsUseCase
database "own database" as DBAR
end box
collections "peer replicas\nairports-routes-m" as PAR
== GET /api/airports/statistics/busiest ==
Actor -> EAR : GET /api/airports/statistics/busiest\n(HTTPS, Authorization: Bearer JWT)
EAR -> AirportController : to a ready replica\n(another one if it fails)
AirportController -> GetAirportStatisticsUseCase : execute(...)
GetAirportStatisticsUseCase -> DBAR : own routes
GetAirportStatisticsUseCase -> PAR : GET /internal/replicas/routes\n(every peer in parallel)
PAR --> GetAirportStatisticsUseCase : their routes
GetAirportStatisticsUseCase -> DBAR : airports (catalog, complete here)
GetAirportStatisticsUseCase -> GetAirportStatisticsUseCase : keep the latest change of each record,\nleave out deleted ones; filter, compute, sort, page
GetAirportStatisticsUseCase --> AirportController : result
AirportController --> Actor : 200 OK (X-Node-Id; X-Partial-Result if both holders of a record were unreachable)
@enduml
